              {
                "id": "yv5hgr3hot6b88p",
                "text": "Key Equations"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4101859367",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Coming soon"
              }
            ],
            "id": "jjw2p4ric5cewdc",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "smo8ehxr448akna",
                "text": "Key Terms"
              }
            ],
            "id": "dgjdx40q0tvuyca",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "common ion effect"
              },
              {
                "text": " The effect on an existing equilibrium when a substance containing an ion in common with the dissolved species is added to the solution; causes a decrease in the solubility of an ionic species or a decrease in the ionization of a weak acid or base."
              }
            ],
            "id": "317638834",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "complex ion"
              },
              {
                "text": " An ion consisting of a central (usually transition metal) atom or ion surrounded by molecules or ions, called ligands, often via coordinate covalent bonds."
              }
            ],
            "id": "192689855",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "coordinate covalent bonds"
              },
              {
                "text": " A covalent bond in which both electrons originated from the same atom. Also called dative bond."
              }
            ],
            "id": "4148940864",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "dissociation constant ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "term": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "term": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": ")"
              },
              {
                "text": " Equilibrium constant for the decomposition of a complex ion into its components; it is the inverse of the formations constant ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": ")."
              }
            ],
            "id": "244850298",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "dissolution"
              },
              {
                "text": " The process of dissolving."
              }
            ],
            "id": "2013165288",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "formation constant ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "term": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "term": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": ")"
              },
              {
                "text": " Equilibrium constant for the formation of a complex ion from its components. Also called stability constant."
              }
            ],
            "id": "1870753552",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "homogeneous mixture"
              },
              {
                "text": " A mixture that has a uniform composition and appears visually the same throughout."
              }
            ],
            "id": "65976920",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "hydrothermal precipitation"
              },
              {
                "text": " The precipitation of solids from hot mineral-laden water (hydrothermal solution)."
              }
            ],
            "id": "1899339848",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "ligand"
              },
              {
                "text": " A molecule or ion that bonds to the central atom of a complex ion by donating one or more electron pairs."
              }
            ],
            "id": "4029659",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "precipitate"
              },
              {
                "text": " Verb: To cause a substance to separate from a solution as a solid."
              }
            ],
            "id": "897945978",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "precipitation"
              },
              {
                "text": " The formation of an insoluble solid from a supersaturated solution."
              }
            ],
            "id": "286955804",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "saturated"
              },
              {
                "text": " Describes a solution that contains the maximum concentration of solute possible for a given temperature and pressure; of concentration equal to solubility."
              }
            ],
            "id": "2549822258",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "selective precipitation"
              },
              {
                "text": " A technique for separating ions in an aqueous solution using differences in their solubility with a given precipitating reagent."
              }
            ],
            "id": "616822993",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "solubility product constant ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "term": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "term": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": ")"
              },
              {
                "text": " Equilibrium constant for the dissolution of an ionic compound."
              }
            ],
            "id": "4197080801",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "term": true,
                "text": "supersaturated"
              },
              {
                "text": " Describes a solution containing more than the maximum concentration of a solute dissolved in a solvent (a nonequilibrium state)."
              }
            ],
            "id": "eup76naq6gev6ne",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "editor": "slate",
